H2200.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2199 (זָעַק);
to make an outcry
KJV: cry.

H2201.definition:
and (feminine) זְעָקָהxlit zᵉâqâh corrected to zᵉʻâqâh; from H2199 (זָעַק);
a shriek or outcry
KJV: cry(-ing).

H2202.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to be fragrant);
Ziphron, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ziphron.

H2203.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to liquify);
asphalt (from its tendency to soften in the sun)
KJV: pitch.

H2204.definition:
a primitive root;
to be old
KJV: aged man, be (wax) old (man).

H2205.definition:
from H2204 (זָקֵן);
old
KJV: aged, ancient (man), elder(-est), old (man, men and...women), senator.

H2206.definition:
from H2204 (זָקֵן);
the beard (as indicating age)
KJV: beard.

H2207.definition:
from H2204 (זָקֵן);
old age
KJV: age.

H2208.definition:
properly, passive participle of H2204 (זָקֵן) (used only in the plural as a noun);
old age
KJV: old age.

H2209.definition:
feminine of H2205 (זָקֵן);
old age
KJV: old (age).

H2210.definition:
a primitive root;
to life, i.e. (figuratively) comfort
KJV: raise (up).

H2211.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2210 (זָקַף);
to hang, i.e. impale
KJV: set up.

H2212.definition:
a primitive root;
to strain, (figuratively) extract, clarify
KJV: fine, pour down, purge, purify, refine.

H2213.definition:
from H2237 (זָרַר) (in the sense of scattering);
a chaplet (as spread around the top), i.e. (specifically) a border moulding
KJV: crown.

H2214.definition:
from H2114 (זוּר) (in the sense of estrangement) (compare H2219 (זָרָה));
disgust
KJV: loathsome.

H2215.definition:
a primitive root;
to flow away
KJV: wax warm.

H2216.definition:
from H2215 (זָרַב) and H894 (בָּבֶל); descended of (i.e. from) Babylon, i.e. born there;
Zerubbabel, an Israelite
KJV: Zerubbabel.

H2217.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2216 (זְרֻבָּבֶל)
{Zerubbabel, an Israelite}
KJV: Zerubbabel.

H2218.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be exuberant in growth; lined with shrubbery;
Zered, a brook East of the Dead Sea
KJV: Zared, Zered.

H2219.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2114 (זוּר));
to toss about; by implication, to diffuse, winnow
KJV: cast away, compass, disperse, fan, scatter (away), spread, strew, winnow.

H2220.definition:
or (shortened) זְרֹעַ; and (feminine) זְרוֹעָה; or זְרֹעָה; from H2232 (זָרַע);
the arm (as stretched out), or (of animals) the foreleg; figuratively, force
KJV: arm, [phrase] help, mighty, power, shoulder, strength.

H2221.definition:
from H2232 (זָרַע);
something sown, i.e. a plant
KJV: sowing, thing that is sown.

H2222.definition:
by reduplication from an unused root meaning to flow;
a pouring rain
KJV: water.

H2223.definition:
by reduplication from H2115 (זוּר);
properly, tightly girt, i.e. probably a racer, or some fleet animal (as being slender in the waist)
KJV: [phrase] greyhound.

H2224.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to irradiate (or shoot forth beams), i.e. to rise (as the sun); specifically, to appear (as a symptom of leprosy)
KJV: arise, rise (up), as soon as it is up.

H2225.definition:
from H2224 (זָרַח);
a rising of light
KJV: rising.

H2226.definition:
the same as H2225 (זֶרַח);
Zerach, the name of three Israelites, also of an Idumaean and an Ethiopian prince
KJV: Zarah, Zerah.

H2227.definition:
patronymically from H2226 (זֶרַח);
a Zarchite or descendant of Zerach
KJV: Zarchite.

H2228.definition:
from H2225 (זֶרַח) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has risen;
Zerachjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Zerahiah.

H2229.definition:
a primitive root;
to gush (as water)
KJV: carry away as with a flood, pour out.

H2230.definition:
from H2229 (זָרַם);
a gush of water
KJV: flood, overflowing, shower, storm, tempest.

H2231.definition:
feminine of H2230 (זֶרֶם);
a gushing of fluid (semen)
KJV: issue.

H2232.definition:
a primitive root;
to sow; figuratively, to disseminate, plant, fructify
KJV: bear, conceive seed, set with sow(-er), yield.

H2233.definition:
from H2232 (זָרַע);
seed; figuratively, fruit, plant, sowing-time, posterity
KJV: [idiom] carnally, child, fruitful, seed(-time), sowing-time.

H2234.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2233 (זֶרַע);
posterity
KJV: seed.

H2235.definition:
or זֵרָעֹן; from H2232 (זָרַע);
something sown (only in the plural), i.e. a vegetable (as food)
KJV: pulse.

H2236.definition:
a primitive root;
to sprinkle (fluid or solid particles)
KJV: be here and there, scatter, sprinkle, strew.

H2237.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2114 (זוּר));
perhaps to diffuse, i.e. (specifically) to sneeze
KJV: sneeze.

H2238.definition:
of Persian origin;
Zeresh, Haman's wife
KJV: Zeresh.

H2239.definition:
from H2219 (זָרָה);
the spread of the fingers, i.e. a span
KJV: span.

H2240.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Zattu, an Israelite
KJV: Zattu.

H2241.definition:
apparently a variation for H2133 (זֵיתָן);
Zetham, an Israelite
KJV: Zetham.

H2242.definition:
of Persian origin;
Zethar, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Zethar. j

H2243.definition:
by contraction from H2245 (חָבַב);
properly, a cherisher, i.e. the bosom
KJV: bosom.

H2244.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2245 (חָבַב));
to secrete
KJV: [idiom] held, hide (self), do secretly.

H2245.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2244 (חָבָא), H2247 (חָבָה));
properly, to hide (as in the bosom), i.e. to cherish (with affection)
KJV: love.

H2246.definition:
from H2245 (חָבַב); cherished;
Chobab, father-in-law of Moses
KJV: Hobab.

H2247.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2245 (חָבַב));
to secrete
KJV: hide (self).

H2248.definition:
(Aramaic) from H2255 (חֲבַל);
properly, overthrown, i.e. (morally) crime
KJV: hurt.

H2249.definition:
from H2266 (חָבַר); united;
Chabor, a river of Assyria
KJV: Habor.

H2250.definition:
or חַבֻּרָה; or חֲבֻרָה; from H2266 (חָבַר);
properly, bound (with stripes), i.e. a weal (or black-and-blue mark itself)
KJV: blueness, bruise, hurt, stripe, wound.

H2251.definition:
a primitive root;
to knock out or off
KJV: beat (off, out), thresh.

H2252.definition:
or חֲבָיָהlemma חֲבָיה missing vowel, corrected to חֲבָיָה; from H2247 (חָבָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has hidden;
Chabajah, an Israelite
KJV: Habaiah.

H2253.definition:
from H2247 (חָבָה);
a concealment
KJV: hiding.

H2254.definition:
a primitive root;
to wind tightly (as a rope), i.e. to bind; specifically, by a pledge; figuratively, to pervert, destroy; also to writhe in pain (especially of parturition)
KJV: [idiom] at all, band, bring forth, (deal) corrupt(-ly), destroy, offend, lay to (take a) pledge, spoil, travail, [idiom] very, withhold.

H2255.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2254 (חָבַל);
to ruin
KJV: destroy, hurt.

H2256.definition:
or חֵבֶל; from H2254 (חָבַל);
a rope (as twisted), especially a measuring line; by implication, a district or inheritance (as measured); or a noose (as of cords); figuratively, a company (as if tied together); also a throe (especially of parturition); also ruin
KJV: band, coast, company, cord, country, destruction, line, lot, pain, pang, portion, region, rope, snare, sorrow, tackling.

H2257.definition:
(Aramaic) from H2255 (חֲבַל);
harm (personal or pecuniary)
KJV: damage, hurt.

H2258.definition:
or (feminine) חֲבֹלָה; from H2254 (חָבַל);
a pawn (as security for debt)
KJV: pledge.

H2259.definition:
active participle from H2254 (חָבַל) (in the sense of handling ropes);
a sailor
KJV: pilot, shipmaster.

H2260.definition:
from H2254 (חָבַל) (in the sense of furnished with ropes);
a mast
KJV: mast.

H2261.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
probably meadow-saffron
KJV: rose.

H2262.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Chabatstsanjah, a Rechabite
KJV: Habazaniah.

H2263.definition:
a primitive root;
to clasp (the hands or in embrace)
KJV: embrace, fold.

H2264.definition:
from H2263 (חָבַק);
a clasping of the hands (in idleness)
KJV: fold.

H2265.definition:
by reduplication from H2263 (חָבַק); embrace;
Chabakkuk, the prophet
KJV: Habakkuk.

H2266.definition:
a primitive root;
to join (literally or figuratively); specifically (by means of spells) to fascinate
KJV: charm(-er), be compact, couple (together), have fellowship with, heap up, join (self, together), league.

H2267.definition:
from H2266 (חָבַר);
a society; also a spell
KJV: [phrase] charmer(-ing), company, enchantment, [idiom] wide.

H2268.definition:
the same as H2267 (חֶבֶר); community;
Cheber, the name of a Kenite and of three Israelites
KJV: Heber.

H2269.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2266 (חָבַר);
an associate
KJV: companion, fellow.

H2270.definition:
from H2266 (חָבַר);
an associate
KJV: companion, fellow, knit together.

H2271.definition:
from H2266 (חָבַר);
a partner
KJV: companion.

H2272.definition:
by reduplication from H2266 (חָבַר);
a streak (like a line), as on the tiger
KJV: spot.

H2273.definition:
(Aramaic) feminine of H2269 (חֲבַר);
an associate
KJV: other.

H2274.definition:
feminine of H2267 (חֶבֶר);
association
KJV: company.

H2275.definition:
from H2267 (חֶבֶר); seat of association;
Chebron, a place in Palestine, also the name of two Israelites
KJV: Hebron.

H2276.definition:
or חֶבְרֹנִי; patronymically from H2275 (חֶבְרוֹן);
Chebronite (collectively), an inhabitant of Chebron
KJV: Hebronites.

H2277.definition:
patronymically from H2268 (חֶבֶר);
a Chebrite (collectively) or descendants of Cheber
KJV: Heberites.

H2278.definition:
feminine of H2270 (חָבֵר);
a consort
KJV: companion.

H2279.definition:
feminine active participle of H2266 (חָבַר);
a joint
KJV: which coupleth, coupling.

H2280.definition:
a primitive root;
to wrap firmly (especially a turban, compress, or saddle); figuratively, to stop, to rule
KJV: bind (up), gird about, govern, healer, put, saddle, wrap about.

H2281.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to cook (compare H4227 (מַחֲבַת));
something fried, probably a griddle-cake
KJV: pan.

H2282.definition:
or חָג; from H2287 (חָגַג);
a festival, or a victim therefor
KJV: (solemn) feast (day), sacrifice, solemnity.

H2283.definition:
from an unused root meaning to revolve (compare H2287 (חָגַג));
properly, vertigo, i.e. (figuratively) fear
KJV: terror.

H2284.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a locust
KJV: locust.

H2285.definition:
the same as H2284 (חָגָב); locust;
Chagab, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Hagab.

H2286.definition:
or חֲגָבָה; feminine of H2285 (חָגָב); locust;
Chagaba or Chagabah, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Hagaba, Hagabah.

H2287.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2283 (חָגָא), H2328 (חוּג));
properly, to move in acircle, i.e. (specifically) to march in asacred procession, to observe afestival; by implication, to be giddy
KJV: celebrate, dance, (keep, hold) a (solemn) feast (holiday), reel to and fro.

H2288.definition:
from an unused root meaning to take refuge;
a rift in rocks
KJV: cleft.

H2289.definition:
from H2296 (חָגַר);
belted
KJV: girded with.

H2290.definition:
or חֲגֹר; and (feminine) חֲגוֹרָה; or חֲגֹרָה; from H2296 (חָגַר);
a belt (for the waist)
KJV: apron, armour, gird(-le).

H2292.definition:
from H2282 (חַג); festive;
Chaggai, a Hebrew prophet
KJV: Haggai.

H2293.definition:
from H2282 (חַג) and H3050 (יָהּ); festival of Jah;
Chaggijah, an Israelite
KJV: Haggiah.

H2294.definition:
feminine of H2291 (חַגִּי); festive;
Chaggith, a wife of David
KJV: Haggith.

H2295.definition:
of uncertain derivation; probably a partridge;
Choglah, an Israelitess
KJV: Hoglah. See also H1031 (בֵּית חׇגְלָה).

H2296.definition:
a primitive root;
to gird on (as a belt, armor, etc.)
KJV: be able to put on, be afraid, appointed, gird, restrain, [idiom] on every side.

H2297.definition:
abridged from H259 (אֶחָד);
one
KJV: one.

H2298.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2297 (חַד);
as card. one; as article single; as an ordinal, first; adverbially, at once
KJV: a, first, one, together.
